implementationPlan.description:
Inventory only; no code. This is the epic-final task. Read every prerequisite's LANDED entry points and its Serena handoff memory, then list in the step note the exact names the tests will call:
- C02b readSnapshotSource;
- C03 semanticSource;
- C04 the positive cache;
- C05 negativeSearch (recordNegative, lookupNegative, the generations);
- C06a and C06: contextDelta, and get_context's basePacketId and contextEpoch;
- C07 planReuseJob, with claim and get_context planReuse;
- C08 recipe.ts: instantiateRecipe, recipeKinds, RECIPE_ACTOR and readRecipeInstance;
- C09 docsLiteralReplace, including assessPostpatch;
- C11a: the docs.
Where a landed name differs from the planned one, use the landed one. Error handling: if a prerequisite is missing an entry point the matrix needs, call moe.report_blocked naming that task; never stub it in a test.

Write packages/moe-daemon/src/__e2e__/contextInvalidation.e2e.test.ts for DoD1. It covers positive, negative, context and recipe invalidation across roles.
- Use real temp Git repos and ToolTestHarness, with GIT_* masked and fixed identities.
- Snapshots come from the landed scripts/local-runner/source-export.mjs, under describe.skipIf when scripts/ is absent.
- Assert exact statuses and reasons; table-driven.

Cases:
- P (C04): a cached read is invalidated by a dirty byte change while `git status --porcelain` stays byte-identical. A relevant config or lockfile change invalidates only its slice.
- N (C05):
  - a recorded zero-match search goes 'stale' when an untracked helper is added in scope;
  - deleting the helper also makes it 'stale';
  - a truncated or incomplete enumeration is 'unknown', never 'absent';
  - a fresh store (restart) is 'unknown'.
- S (C03): an absent or failed analyzer is inconclusive with a literal fallback, and is never recorded as a negative.
- D (C06):
  - the worker session gets a delta with explicit removals;
  - QA and architect reads with no running attempt get a full snapshot;
  - restart, reattach, epoch change, a different session and a re-claim each give a full snapshot with their exact reasons.
- R (C09):
  - a doc changed after the request falls back with docs-replace-hash-mismatch, and the task stays PLANNING;
  - a changed definition makes assessPostpatch return docs-replace-recipe-mismatch;
  - changed inputs give docs-replace-inputs-changed;
  - under deliveryPolicy 'local-branch', a candidate that edits .moe/recipes.json gets protected-check-changed:.moe/recipes.json.

Full regression, once, fresh. This is the epic final, so run every affected suite in an isolated Linux snapshot of HEAD: whole-repo git archive, native deps, MOE_* unset, Linux-only PATH (mem:gotcha-daemon-linux-snapshot-gate). The suites:
- `cd packages/moe-daemon && npm test` and `npx tsc --noEmit`;
- `npm run lint` at the root, because C10 changed role docs;
- `node --test scripts/tests/prompt-cache-launcher.test.mjs`, which C10 extended;
- `cd packages/moe-proxy && npm test`, only if any CQ-C commit touched packages/moe-proxy. Check with git log --grep 'Moe-Task' over the epic's task ids.
Every suite must exit 0. Supply the daemon npm test command, exit code and output tail to complete_task, and list the other results in the summary.

Whole-epic adversarial review, the last step (load adversarial-self-review). Sweep the ENTIRE CQ-C diff: every epic task's commits on moe/work-2026-10-24, plus C11a's docs read against the code. Check:
- any approval bypass, or a re-stamped approval;
- a planner skipped outside valid reuse or an eligible recipe;
- scope expansion past the approved plan;
- stale context served as fresh;
- a cache answering 'absent' on incomplete enumeration, or freshness taken from watchers or status;
- a delta served across an incarnation;
- recipe identity impersonation, or a definition changeable without approval;
- forbidden-pattern tokens, .moe edits, and Git writes outside the wrappers.
Fix small issues within step 4's rules, and list the rest as findings. In the completion summary, list the activation items still deliberately open:
- the call site for assessPostpatch;
- seat-side contextEpoch stamping (the compaction keeper and the proxy);
- C02/C03 providers in served packets.
These belong to the rollout (M05/M06), not to C11. Write the epic handoff memory.

